["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIGa0e225f0fa79f94f748948d5ab8652212b1e578a28fc226891c3055b3c33da0b","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/redact-covers-home-and-user","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: `--redact` covers the home directory and the user name\n\n## Outcome\n\nA recorded stream can be committed to a public repository: no absolute home path and no local user name survive redaction, and the manifest's digest is taken after redaction so the file still ingests.\n\n## Context\n\nThe eight P1 streams recorded on 2026-09-03 under `--redact` carried `/home/<user>` 18–49 times each and the user name 20–51 times, so none of them could go into the public `recorded/` directories the cases were written for; they stay on the operator's machine.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `--redact` replaces the operator's home directory with `~` (or `<home>`) and the user name with `<user>` in every event text and path field; the rule is documented beside the existing redaction rules.\n- The transcript digest in the manifest is computed over the redacted bytes, so `aep eval run --stream` accepts the file.\n- A test feeds a stream containing both and asserts neither survives; an ingestion test proves the redacted file replays.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nRedacting repository names or commit ids; those are the run's subject.\n\n## Ambiguities\n\n- `inferable` — where redaction lives today: the `--redact` path in `crates/protocol-cli/src/eval.rs`.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone.\n","owner":"eval","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:self-evaluation"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Recorded streams carried /home/<user> and the user name 18–51 times each; redact them and digest after, so a stream can be committed to a public recorded/ directory.","tags":["eval"],"title":"--redact covers the home directory and the user name"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIGa0e225f0fa79f94f748948d5ab8652212b1e578a28fc226891c3055b3c33da0b","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIGa0e225f0fa79f94f748948d5ab8652212b1e578a28fc226891c3055b3c33da0b"]}]